---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Wave from "../components/Wave.astro";
import { urls } from "../data/homepage";
import { edgeAbove } from "../data/edge-line";
import caseV from "../assets/cases/case-study-v-founder-life-after-exit.png";

const grass = "#E7FFF6";
const heroEdge = edgeAbove("#2A0B4F");
const bandEdge = edgeAbove(grass);
const joinEdge = edgeAbove("#ffffff");
---

<Base
  title="Clarity-First Guarantee | DoGood Agency"
  description="Founder Reclamation Partnership | Stage 1: The Intensive (30 days)"
  canonical="https://www.dogoodagency.co/clarity-first-guarantee-terms"
  footerStrip={grass}
  footerEdge={bandEdge}
>
  <article class="page-clarity" style={`--band-tint:${grass};--join-edge:${joinEdge}`}>
    <header class="privacy-hero">
      <div class="privacy-hero-inner">
        <h1>Clarity‑First Guarantee (Stage 1)</h1>
      </div>
      <Wave fill={grass} edge={heroEdge} />
    </header>

    <section class="privacy-band privacy-band-tint">
      <div class="privacy-well clarity-intro">
<p>You can’t know whether FRP is right for you from the outside — you only know once you’ve been inside the work.</p>
<p>Complete onboarding and attend your first two private 1:1 sessions.</p>
<p>If you decide this partnership isn’t right for you, email us within 7 calendar days of your first private 1:1 session. We will keep only what covers the two private sessions you have already used — and refund the rest, without questions asked.</p>
<p>If the Stage 1: coach match feels wrong in the first two sessions, we’ll correct it quickly. If we can’t correct it without delay, you can exit via the Clarity‑First Guarantee.</p>
<p>Even if you exit, you keep everything we’ve already done together in those first sessions: the decisions we clarified, the containment plan we set, and any tools or written notes we shared along the way.</p>
<p>We take real delivery risk here on purpose, because we only want to continue if it’s genuinely the right fit.</p>
<p>Seb Wichmann | Founder, DoGood Agency</p>
        <picture class="clarity-sketch">
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/sketches/clarity-first-guarantee-folder@1x.webp 540w, /sketches/clarity-first-guarantee-folder@2x.webp 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) min(100vw, 420px), 420px" />
          <img src="/sketches/clarity-first-guarantee-folder@1x.png" srcset="/sketches/clarity-first-guarantee-folder@1x.png 540w, /sketches/clarity-first-guarantee-folder@2x.png 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) min(100vw, 420px), 420px" width="540" height="400" alt="" />
        </picture>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="privacy-divider" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="privacy-divider-wave" style={`--wave-edge:${bandEdge}`} viewBox="0 0 1440 80" preserveAspectRatio="none">
        <path fill="#ffffff" d="M0 48c180 32 320-40 520-24s300 56 480 24 280-56 440-16v48H0Z"></path>
        <path class="wave-edge" d="M0 48c180 32 320-40 520-24s300 56 480 24 280-56 440-16"></path>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <section class="privacy-band privacy-band-white">
      <div class="privacy-well">
        <section id="case-v" aria-label="Case study">
          <article class="card case-compact case-v">
            <img class="portrait" src={caseV.src} width="220" height="244" alt="Pixelated portrait of founder V, shown this way to protect their identity" />
            <div>
              <p class="t-kicker">Case Study</p>
              <h3>From identity void to decisive leadership —<br />How V reclaimed life after success</h3>
              <p class="caption case-who">V (anonymous), USD 9M+ founder</p>
              <div class="btn-stack">
                <a class="btn-case" href={urls.caseV}>Read the short case study</a>
                <p class="case-protect">We protect our founders’ identities</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-band privacy-band-tint">
      <div class="privacy-well clarity-terms">
<p>Terms & Conditions</p>
<p>Last updated: Feb 9th 2026</p>
<p>1. Definitions</p>
<ul>
  <li>"Stage 1" means FRP — Stage 1: The Reset (30 days)</li>
  <li>"Stage 1 / Session 1 / Day 1" means the client’s first live (virtual) private 1:1 session (not the acceptance call, payment date, or onboarding date).</li>
  <li>"Onboarding” means the onboarding starter pack + intake/ setup steps, which occur before or around the start of Stage 1 delivery.</li>
  <li>“In‑Person Intensive” means the 1.5‑day in‑person working block that is part of Stage 1 (travel to the client’s location).</li>
</ul>
<p>2. Eligibility requirements The Clarity‑First Guarantee applies only if the client:</p>
<ul>
  <li>completes onboarding requirements in full, and</li>
  <li>attends the first two private 1:1 sessions, and</li>
  <li>exits within the required timeframe during the guarantee window (see below)</li>
</ul>
<p>3. Guarantee window The client may exit by emailing DoGood within 7 calendar days of Session 1.</p>
<p>If the client exits inside the Clarity‑First window:</p>
<ul>
  <li>DoGood will keep only the portion of the Stage 1 investment that covers the two private sessions already delivered.</li>
  <li>DoGood will refund the remainder.</li>
</ul>
<p>“Without questions asked” definition “Without questions asked” means: DoGood does not interrogate, debate, or require justification for the client’s decision. The client simply emails within the window and, provided the above eligibility requirements are met, DoGood processes the refund accordingly.</p>
<p>Work completed remains with the client If the client exits inside the guarantee window, the client keeps the work completed in the first two sessions (including decisions clarified, containment plan set, and any tools or written notes shared during delivery). DoGood does not request the return or deletion of materials provided during delivery.</p>
<p>3. In‑person intensive exclusion (Stage 1)</p>
<p>The Clarity‑First Guarantee applies only before any in‑person intensive is initiated or scheduled. If an in‑person intensive has been scheduled, initiated, or incurred costs (e.g., travel booking), the Clarity‑First Guarantee no longer applies, and any refund eligibility (if any) must be handled as a separate written exception approved by DoGood.</p>
<p>4. Coach match correction (Stage 1)</p>
<p>If, within the first two sessions, the client believes the coach match feels wrong, DoGood will attempt to correct the match promptly. If DoGood cannot correct the match without delay or disruption, the client may choose to exit via the Clarity‑First Guarantee, provided they are still within the 7‑day window and all eligibility requirements are met.</p>
<p>5. Refund processing mechanics</p>
<p>Refunds are processed to the original payment method on file only.</p>
<p>6. Priority Hold and delayed starts</p>
<p>If the client is entering via a Priority Hold (seat reservation), the Priority Hold deposit terms and start-date clauses apply as defined in the Priority Hold mechanism (separate from the Clarity‑First Guarantee).</p>
<p>7. Confidentiality</p>
<p>FRP is private and confidential (“no groups, no cohorts”), and confidentiality terms are provided during onboarding as part of the engagement policies.</p>
<p>8. How to invoke the guarantee</p>
<p>To invoke the Clarity‑First Guarantee, email: <a href="mailto:hiya@dogoodagency.co?subject=Clarity%E2%80%91First%20Guarantee%20%E2%80%94%20Exit%20Request">hiya@dogoodagency.co</a> | Subject: Clarity‑First Guarantee — Exit Request | Include: your full name + date of Session 1.</p>
<a class="btn-teal" href="/">Back To Homepage</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
